## Equipment setup
## Coy chamber for anaerobic protein self-assembly setup
The anaerobic chamber should be maintained in an oxygen-free (or very low oxygen) atmosphere (e.g., a mix of $10\%$ $\mathrm{H}_{2}/90\%$ Ar). Self-assembly buffers are prepared in an anaerobic environment and degassed prior to storage in an anaerobic Coy chamber. Transition metal salts used for self-assembly are taken into the Coy chamber as solid salts in Eppendorf tubes and dissolved into degassed $\mathrm{\ddH}_{2}\mathrm{O}$ . To set up self-assembly conditions, a stock solution of protein $\mathrm{^{\prime}10{-}20\ \upmu L})$ was taken into the anaerobic chamber and diluted with degassed buffers.
## ESI-MS analysis
Small molecule samples are dissolved in methanol and diluted to a concentration of $0.1\mathrm{{-}1.0\ m g/m L}$ using a solution of $50\%$ methanol in water. Protein samples are buffer exchanged into water using Amicon spin filters and diluted to a concentration of $0.1\mathrm{-}1.0~\mathrm{mg/mL}$ using a solution of $0.1\%$ TFA and $50\%$ methanol in water.
## FPLC for protein purification
Equilibrate a Q-cartridge at $3\mathrm{mL}/\mathrm{min}$ in FPLC Buffer A for ${\sim}10$ column volumes prior to loading any protein onto the column. Proteins are loaded using either a $5~\mathrm{mL}$ sample loop or a $90~\mathrm{mL}$ DynaLoop and eluted using a linear gradient of $\mathrm{\DeltaNaCl}$ at $3\ \mathrm{mL}/\mathrm{min}$ . Clean the Q column with ${\sim}10$ column volumes of FPLC Buffer B, and equilibrate in FPLC Buffer A prior to the application of additional protein solutions.
## NMR analysis
$\mathrm{^{1}H}$ and $^{13}\mathrm{C}$ spectra are collected at ${\sim}25~^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ in DMSO- $\cdot\mathbf{d}_{6}$ . NMR chemical shifts (relative to tetramethylsilane) are 2.49 ${}^{(^{1}\mathrm{H)}}$ and 39.5 ${}^{(^{13}\mathrm{C)}}$ for DMSO- $\cdot\mathbf{d}_{6}$ . MestReNova software (Mestrelab Research) is used for spectral analysis.
## Procedure 1: HA-mediated protein cages
## Preparation of O-tritylhydroxylamine $0$ Timing 10–12 h
1 Prepare a $250~\mathrm{mL}$ RB flask with a magnetic stir bar and $50~\mathrm{mL}$ of DMF as the solvent. ! CAUTION DMF is a skin irritant, carcinogenic and toxic. Wear goggles and gloves, and work inside a fume hood to avoid breathing in vapors.   
